<%# locals: owner:, name:, subscription:, error: (optional)

    Watching a repository from the repository's own page — the same thing the
    form on /subscriptions does, from where someone actually stands when they
    decide they want it.

    It posts to the same two actions, with `from: "repo"`, which is what tells
    WebhookSubscriptionsController to send this control back in place instead
    of redirecting to /subscriptions. Every failure the registrar can raise
    lands in `error:` and is rendered right here, next to the control that
    caused it.

    **One control with states, not a pile of controls.** Whatever Prism is
    doing with this repository, the header holds exactly one `.btn`-shaped
    thing next to "Open on GitHub": "Watch repository" when it is doing
    nothing, and the state itself — Watching / Not working / Wrong address —
    when it is. Same shape, same height, so the header does not jump when
    someone watches or unwatches, and one line at every width the two fit on.

    Watching is a deliberate second click through a confirmation dialog,
    because it edits pull requests under this person's name (see
    confirm_dialog_controller.js). Unwatching is reversible, so it is a quiet
    item inside the state's own menu rather than a red button in the header. %>
<% error = local_assigns[:error] %>
<%# No `flex-auto`: the control is sized by its content and packs against
    "Open on GitHub" rather than growing to push itself to the far end of
    the row. %>
<div id="repo-watch" class="flex min-w-0 flex-col items-end gap-1.5 text-right"
     data-testid="repo-watch">
  <% if subscription %>
    <%= render "webhook_subscriptions/watch_menu", subscription: subscription %>
  <% else %>
    <%# `flex`, so the button is a flex item rather than an inline one: an
        inline-flex button sits on its parent's text baseline, and the strut
        under it made this state two pixels taller than the watching one. %>
    <%= form_with url: webhook_subscriptions_path, method: :post, class: "flex",
                  data: { controller: "confirm-dialog", testid: "watch-form" } do |form| %>
      <%= form.hidden_field :full_name, value: "#{owner}/#{name}" %>
      <%= form.hidden_field :from, value: "repo" %>

      <button type="submit" class="btn-primary"
              data-confirm-dialog-target="trigger"
              data-action="confirm-dialog#open"
              data-testid="repo-watch-button">Watch repository</button>

      <%# `m-auto` is not decoration: Preflight zeroes every margin, which
          includes the `margin: auto` the UA stylesheet uses to centre a
          modal dialog, so without it the dialog sits in the top left. %>
      <dialog class="m-auto w-[calc(100vw-2rem)] max-w-md rounded-xl border border-line bg-surface p-0 text-ink shadow-lg shadow-ink/10 backdrop:bg-canvas/70 backdrop:backdrop-blur-sm"
              aria-labelledby="watch-dialog-title"
              data-confirm-dialog-target="dialog"
              data-action="click->confirm-dialog#cancelOnBackdrop close->confirm-dialog#restoreFocus"
              data-testid="watch-dialog">
        <div class="max-h-[80vh] overflow-y-auto p-5 text-left">
          <h2 id="watch-dialog-title" class="font-display text-base font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">
            Watch <%= owner %>/<%= name %>?
          </h2>

          <div class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-soft">
            <%= render "webhook_subscriptions/consent", login: current_user.login %>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap justify-end gap-2">
            <button type="button" class="btn-secondary"
                    data-action="confirm-dialog#cancel"
                    data-testid="watch-cancel">Cancel</button>
            <button type="submit" class="btn-primary"
                    data-confirm-dialog-target="confirm"
                    data-testid="watch-confirm">Watch repository</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </dialog>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>

  <%# What is printed under the control is only ever exceptional: a failure,
      or a subscription that has stopped working. Neither is something to
      tuck inside a menu — they are the reason someone would open it.
      The width cap is what keeps the row a row: the header's action slot is
      `shrink-0`, so an uncapped sentence claims the width of the sentence
      and shoves the control onto a line of its own. %>
  <% if error.present? %>
    <p role="alert" class="max-w-72 text-sm text-removed sm:max-w-sm" data-testid="repo-watch-error"><%= error %></p>
  <% elsif subscription %>
    <div class="max-w-72 sm:max-w-sm">
      <%= render "webhook_subscriptions/status_reason", subscription: subscription %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
